<%# ONE TEAM'S TIMEOUTS, drawn as the bar at the left of its row on the hero
    tile. Locals: game (Game), team (Team).

    THREE SEGMENTS, one per timeout, lit while the team still holds it — so
    the count sits beside the team it belongs to rather than in a legend
    somewhere else. Spent ones go dark from the TOP, so what is left reads as
    a level.

    Only while the game is being played and the feed is counting. Otherwise it
    is the plain bar it always was, because a scheduled game has spent nothing
    and a final one has nothing left to spend.

    The tile gives the wrapper the id game_<slug>_timeouts_<team slug>, and
    Contest::LiveBroadcast.plays_changed updates what is inside it. %>
<%
  accent = team_card_palette(team)[:accent]
  left = team&.slug == game.home_team_slug ? game.home_timeouts : game.away_timeouts
%>
<% if game.live? && left %>
  <span class="flex flex-col gap-1 h-full w-full" data-test="live-focus-timeouts"
        data-team-slug="<%= team&.slug %>" data-timeouts="<%= left %>"
        role="img" aria-label="<%= pluralize(left, "timeout") %> left"
        title="<%= pluralize(left, "timeout") %> left">
    <% 3.times do |segment| %>
      <span class="flex-1 rounded-full"
            style="background: <%= segment >= 3 - left ? accent : "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22)" %>"></span>
    <% end %>
  </span>
<% else %>
  <span class="block h-full w-full rounded-full" style="background: <%= accent %>"></span>
<% end %>
